Spec: Portable pending registration transactions

Purpose:
  Atomically retain caller-scoped unapproved declarations and operation results through a supplied SQL session port.

Owns:
  ./PendingRegistry.java

Must:
  Commit the normalized pending declaration and successful operation result in one transaction.
  Deduplicate caller and operation UUID before quota checks; conflict on changed canonical parameters and preserve old results.
  Match the Windows pending result shape and keep approvalRequired `true` without creating grants or flows.
  Retain all results, cap caller operations at `500000`, global operations at `1000000` and registrations at `1024`.
  Use Android26-compatible SQLite syntax, bound parameters and explicit schema checks.
  Convert corrupt stored data and session failures to fixed storage errors without raw exceptions.
